 "verdict": "include",
 "verdict_reason": "Independent-screen replication: labels from the 2022 screen scored by 2023 AUROC 0.975, reverse 0.943 (Spearman 0.36); replicates 0.88-0.97. Orientation split (AB-only vs BA-only) is weak (0.65-0.70, Spearman 0.10-0.14; AB-2022 correlates better with AB-2023 than with BA-2022, i.e. a reproducible sgRNA-position effect), which is why the orientation-averaged score is used. Cross-study K562 vs horlbeck2018: our score for their labels 0.731 (97 pos); their score for our labels 0.875 but only 14 pos; vs herken2026 0.97/0.95 (170/165 pos), same lab lineage so partly non-independent. Hit rate 0.36% (strict end of plausible); fitness-only AUROC 0.62 (screen singles) / 0.50 (DepMap). Caveats: still a preprint; CRISPRi hypomorphic; 23 of 97 horlbeck2018 positives in the overlap fall in our negative band (and 6 are shared positives), so the builder's cross-source conflict rule will blank some pairs."
}